{"title":"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the lengths of the sides of a triangle. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fcaedd680c4342fdcb088fbfe889483ad8250ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^{2}b(a - b) + b^{2}c(b - c) + c^{2}a(c - a)\\ge 0.\\]\" width=\"313\" height=\"20\" />\nDetermine when equality occurs.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Ravi substitution, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4b0cdf9843e48f4cf10318302677fca717b368.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63baf3faa51097650be4bf00a49a2d1b218d7871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = z+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb41b3b69e00188bb6ed1d93c10473967d081ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />. Then, the triangle condition becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/807d636ecb3f86e712c17d898a541eb9296b101a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />. After some manipulation, the inequality becomes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/aff922bfa502ace9eedee7e651296b25db4e3d50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy^3 + yz^3 + zx^3 \\geq xyz(x+y+z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"268\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>By Cauchy, we have: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff2d285010436f0a0124419265b88fb6aeafa00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(xy^3 + yz^3 + zx^3)(z+x+y) \\geq xyz(y+z+x)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"21\" /> with equality if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b302595770233dc95dc66a336a4cb6db8e0899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{xy^3}{z} = \\frac{yz^3}{x} =\\frac{zx^3}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"143\" height=\"44\" />. So the inequality holds with equality if and only if x = y = z. Thus the original inequality has equality if and only if the triangle is equilateral.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b8d5814e4995618285b8897c318b5ceb616b0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\geq b \\geq c &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />. By Muirhead or by AM-GM, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21e0a356f9d7af9b13f7b6c75021ae84c03ad56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 b + a^3 c + b^3 c + b^3 a + c^3 a + c^3 b \\geq 2(a^2 b^2 + a^2 c^2 + b^2 c^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"446\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>If we can show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e5417b7039fb0c1b116b63ce34b58b79ce072ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 b + b^3 c+ c^3 a  \\geq a^3 c +  b^3 a + c^3 b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"261\" height=\"19\" />, we are done, since then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec3c781dd92f8a7cc6b2fab52a94e63cfb18ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(a^3 b + b^3 c+ c^3 a ) \\geq a^3 b + a^3 c + b^3 c + b^3 a + c^3 a + c^3 b \\geq 2(a^2 b^2 + a^2 c^2 + b^2 c^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"611\" height=\"21\" />, and we can divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>We first see that, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901a9e774bf3ab81d1484ba897adf724bcce3f9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2 + ac + c^2) \\geq (b^2 + bc + c^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"239\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09950d8a54ce22304fca56761ad96c4b53e1df4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-c)(b-c)(a^2 + ac + c^2) \\geq (a-c)(b-c)(b^2 + bc + c^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"451\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Factoring, this becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a07a40c16226990f6eee06edd5239bd86478b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^3 - c^3)(b-c) \\geq (a-c)(b^3 - c^3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"268\" height=\"21\" />. This is the same as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b10321a79d1a160be125d08ff6d7e2828abeb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^3 - c^3)(b-c) + (b^3 - c^3)(c-a) \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"299\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Expanding and refactoring, this is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd8cfc5ea9b84f84b0442fb237612ea932a7ac8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 (b-c) + b^3(c-a) + c^3 (a-b) \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"287\" height=\"21\" />. (This step makes more sense going backwards.)\n</p><p>Expanding this out, we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b3daaf7db463135f554c87c94491027a604b207.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3b + b^3 c + c^3 a \\geq a^3 c + b^3 a + c^3 b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"261\" height=\"19\" />,\n</p><p>which is the desired result.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the semiperimeter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a89d18bba1b98335766cb9c78d7a958fb128d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+b+c}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"39\" />, of the triangle. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb5e083ec30dcd286d6aeb0a4e9fd23c88fd852.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=s-\\frac{-a+b+c}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b34b457845d99fd7c0e46f83becd2ac5fa227d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=s-\\frac{a-b+c}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6868522cef283cd716840bab76de93ee922d621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=s-\\frac{a+b-c}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"39\" />. We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a1afa67e351dfd83e048cc7a97569c0698c512.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{-a+b+c}{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"129\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d550d8901492d133605feb429a0e7186c7d08985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{a-b+c}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/774683454dc89c4725582f91dd13f1e2ab85e2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\frac{a+b-c}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"39\" /> (Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> are all positive, since all sides must be shorter than the semiperimeter.) Then, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/a/78a087661ee9bfbdb45df4adf3b5d31bcea41104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=s-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59bb8bdfa886b3030dd96343fbf564bd7a1d724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=s-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d1fb7ba3d1ed44522f330916901383fba2453e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=s-z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b07386c5ca75708dd35a9aa0b2646bbc0c7b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6af65df83c4992c97e63b908c920f234e30972.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=y+z,b=x+z,c=x+y.\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"16\" /> Plugging this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71cb24887ce7146f7c930a46a85a53a65b94b08d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2b(a-b)+b^2c(b-c)+c^2a(c-a)\\geq0\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"20\" /> and doing some expanding and cancellation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90bd6c71e91473423df5c5341732c5be5d3faca4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x^3z+2xy^3+2yz^3-2x^2yz-2xy^2z-2xyz^2\\geq0.\\]\" width=\"392\" height=\"19\" /> The fact that each term on the left hand side has at least two variables multiplied motivates us to divide the inequality by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7adf13d3a44946efaba73797146649d9a6636aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />, which we know is positive from earlier so we can maintain the sign of the inequality. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22c82b9502a5fe4e05114f30fc2c5002b0300aab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^2}{y}-x+\\frac{y^2}{z}-y-z+\\frac{z^2}{x}\\geq0.\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"43\" /> We move the negative terms to the right, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d580fb75b54b60fc93d2432176a024a7d4ae7157.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x^2}{y}+\\frac{y^2}{z}+\\frac{z^2}{x}\\geq x+y+z.\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"43\" /> We rewrite this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e3e516008bf09f789c984f10028252db58258c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{x^2}{y}\\geq\\sum_{cyc}rx+(1-r)y.\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"49\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is any real number. (This works because if we evaulate the cyclic sum, then as long as the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> on the right sum to 1 the right side will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/786294ba81c75be655bda0e12c983b0ef8919a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\"Solution from 111 problems in Algebra and Number Theory\"\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in solution 1, by <b>Ravi's Transformation</b>,  let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4b0cdf9843e48f4cf10318302677fca717b368.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63baf3faa51097650be4bf00a49a2d1b218d7871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = z+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb41b3b69e00188bb6ed1d93c10473967d081ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />. Then, the triangle condition becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/807d636ecb3f86e712c17d898a541eb9296b101a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />. Then,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8dae2c65162552ed955d84ea7b07d23a8ca7b5ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy^3 + yz^3 + zx^3 \\geq xyz(x+y+z)\\]\" width=\"264\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Because the expression is homogenous degree 4, it is sufficient to assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108d7c42600b1f1ea04d17fb59a2e501130ad353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />, from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c49db274dea3d130a4c6cb678378a90a2280f324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{cyc} xy^3 \\geq x+y+z \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"189\" height=\"45\" />. However, this is just trivial via AM-GM, hence the inequality holds. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Equality holds whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9b0046a7446d1f3047baf2c28fd25355f57ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"11\" />, or equivalently <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0ce3f851e9d124ca3388a8bbdebb383a00f9dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b = c$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" /> in the original equality, for when the triangle is equilateral. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO\" title=\"1983 IMO\">1983 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017171019\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 304/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 50/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10837/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.509      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.509      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15673:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017171019 and revision id 287610. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}